    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15559" root="رشح" body-key="r">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارشح</span></b> , intrans.: see 1, first sentence. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْشَحَتْ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>She</i> (a camel, and a woman,) <i>had a
young one that associated,</i> or <i>kept company, with
her, walking with her and behind her, and not
fatiguing her:</i> or <i>had a young one that had
become strong.</i> (L.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ارشحت وَلَدَهَا</span>, said of a
camel: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُرْشِحَ فُلَانٌ لِكَذَا</span>: see 2.

